WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.230
- She's a new mama and Olympic
gold medalist in soccer

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.770
who has been on the forefront
of fighting for equitable pay

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.570
for men and women in sports.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.400
And she's also co-launching

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.990
a new media company called
TOGETHXR just for younger women.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.560
Let's everybody say hi to Alex Morgan.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.510
(audience cheers)

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.343
Hi!

00:00:19.809 --> 00:00:20.980
- Hey Kelly.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.370
- Well, I just saw this video of you

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.250
that you posted of your baby girl.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.373
We're gonna show it.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.163
She's super cute!

00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:31.469
- Aw, thank you.

00:00:31.469 --> 00:00:34.360
She had so much fun, she's a water baby.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.500
- I love that.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.410
I loved the water, I think
it feels rejuvenating.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.030
So any sign she's gonna be into soccer?

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.680
- Oh, she better! No pressure.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.410
But we'll see.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.030
I keep putting a soccer
ball in front of her

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.450
and she wants nothing to do with it.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.820
So hopefully one day.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.040
- Well, how is your prep for
the Tokyo Olympics going?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.040
- Oh, it's good.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.390
I mean, we are in like full prep mode.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.480
And, you know, on the field
every single day getting ready.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.060
And obviously, you know,
looking forward to it so much.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.960
And for me, I kind of get a second chance

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.830
because it would have been really close

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.540
after having my daughter last year.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.160
So, now pushing it to this year,

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.470
I'm really excited for
that second opportunity.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.350
- Yeah. Silver lining.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:20.390
So you have a great new project
that I want to talk about.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:21.450
It's called TOGETHXR.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.490
Can you tell everybody a little about it?

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.650
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.160
So TOGETHXR is a media
company that myself,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.090
Chloe Kim, Simone Manuel,
and Sue Bird co-founded.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.060
And it is a media company

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.060
that really wants to put out
stories and inspire young women

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.270
with these amazing stories
from female athletes.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.170
We've also included culture and fashion

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.910
into that sport lifestyle.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:52.050
So I feel like it's just
all about like empowering

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.650
and encouraging and
motivating girls and women

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.680
to do whatever they want to do.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.110
You know, to go after
their dreams and goals.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.460
- Absolutely.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.480
How has your daughter
deepened your passion

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.810
for gender equality in sports?

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.240
Because I know fighting
for myself is one thing,

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.490
but fighting for your loved one

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:11.960
is a completely different ball game.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.620
So I feel like it got like more so for me.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.670
Do you feel the same?

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.520
- Yeah. I feel like I've
been like full into,

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.780
you know, fighting against
U.S. Soccer, our employer,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.760
for gender equality and for equal pay

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.500
now for the last, ooh
man, five or six years.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.070
So it's been a long time now,

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:39.470
but I feel like it's just
continuing to pick up

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.040
now that I have my daughter

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.470
and now that I'm surrounded by

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.750
so many other inspiring women.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.810
And now that I'm one of
the veterans on the team,

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:48.950
not only do I have my daughter,

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.590
but I have like this next
generation of players

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:52.860
that are coming in

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.390
and like just looking up to
everything that we do and say

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.260
and like what we're fighting for.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:02:59.980
So it's even more important now.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.980
And TOGETHXR also gives me
that platform to be able to

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.440
really change people's like
mindset in knowing that.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.970
And we need guys to support
us as well, you know?

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.400
- I don't think the change will happen

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.360
unless men do support it as well.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.830
I agree with that statement.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.580
I also, like, I don't
watch a ton of sports ball,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.460
which is why I call it sports ball.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.140
But my point is, when I do watch it,

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.410
'cause I have a lot of girlfriends

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.130
and family that love sports.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:26.450
When I do watch it, I find that they,

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.750
I'm like, we just saw this.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:30.130
Like they just showed this
play like 15 minutes ago

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.150
or we just saw this.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.670
And they keep repeating things.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.503
And I'm like,

00:03:33.503 --> 00:03:34.910
I guess for people that
are just now tuning in.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:35.743
But I'm like, okay.

00:03:35.743 --> 00:03:37.890
So my point just from a complete outsider

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.460
is you're not gonna take
away a coverage of the men.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.460
We already saw it.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.320
You just keep playing
it over and over again.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.950
There's room to add the women in there.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.940
And then still everybody
still gets the same.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.110
You're still seeing.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.750
It just seems like they
cover those same things

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.450
over and over which is why
I don't like watching it.

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.520
- That's the thing it's like,
it's not as zero-sum game.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.600
And that's why we created TOGETHXR.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.250
Because, we were like, okay,

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.230
well, if they're not
gonna have space for us

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.480
on the biggest networks,

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.270
then we're gonna create
our own like platform

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.890
to share these stories,

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.790
to show that these women's
stories should be accessible.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.740
You know, growing up,

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.940
I didn't really have professional
athletes on my walls.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.040
I had singers and actresses

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.290
because I didn't know any athletes

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.470
because they weren't on TV.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.090
All I saw were men on TV.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.970
- Yeah. No, I think
representation is super important.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.340
Well, thank you so much, Alex.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.980
Good luck on everything.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.500
- Yeah, thank you so much.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.510
Thanks for having me.
(audience cheers)

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.560
- Yeah. Good luck on mostly being a mama.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:34.560
It's a really cool thing.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.710
It's a hard thing but it's the
coolest thing you'll ever do.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.620
- Yeah. It's tough.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.540
I'm a mom first and athlete
second, but I'm happy with that.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.250
- Absolutely, absolutely

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.900
Well, don't forget to tune
into NBC starting July 23rd

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.450
for all your Olympics coverage.

